import csv
from pathlib import Path
import numpy as np
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];O=R/'ablation_output'
def rd(n):return list(csv.DictReader((O/n).open(encoding='utf-8-sig')))
def avg(rows,k):return float(np.mean([float(x[k]) for x in rows])) if rows else float('nan')
def f(x):return '—' if not np.isfinite(x) else f'{x:.4f}'
lines=['# v1.1 STOI follow-up (report only)','', '**Branch:** `investigate/v1.1-stoi`  ', '**Scope:** report-only. Production DSP, defaults, tags, and merge state were not changed.  ', '**Scores:** STOI and ESTOI (extended STOI) via `pystoi`, 16 kHz mono. `PESQ` was not installable (Cython build requires MSVC); DNSMOS package dependencies installed in a temporary target, but model download from its upstream URL was reset, so no PESQ/DNSMOS scores are claimed.','', '## Summary','', 'The spectral-off/downstream-off cell reproduces the noisy input to numerical precision before PCM export on both sets; PCM WAV rounding changes STOI by under 0.00001. Therefore no fixed stage breaks the all-off identity. The main Classical-route signal is a poorly matched noise PSD: on the original Classical subset its estimated mean power is 12.33× the oracle mean (median 8.48×), and 75.1% of frames selected by VAD as noise overlap clean speech by a -45 dBFS reference mask. With the oracle PSD, STOI is positive vs noisy for both Wiener-only and both spectral stages.','', '## 1. Classical spectral × downstream factorial','', 'Spectral stack “on” means subtraction + adaptive Wiener. Downstream “on” means de-emphasis, aligned EQ, compressor, and normalize/limit. `off_off_pcm` is the all-off float result exported through PCM16. Values below are means; n=14 original, n=12 padded.','', '| Set | Arm | STOI | ΔSTOI vs noisy | ESTOI | ΔESTOI vs noisy | SI-SDR vs noisy (dB) |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in rd('v11b_factorial_summary.csv'):
 if x['arm'] in ('off_off','off_off_pcm','off_on','wiener_on','subtraction_on','both_on'):
  lines.append(f"| {x['dataset']} | {x['arm']} | {f(float(x['mean_stoi']))} | {f(float(x['mean_stoi_delta']))} | {f(float(x['mean_estoi']))} | {f(float(x['mean_estoi_delta']))} | {f(float(x['mean_sisdr_vs_noisy_db']))} |")
lines += ['', 'Identity check: float off/off mean SI-SDR is 140.59 dB original and 140.44 dB padded. PCM16 off/off is 78.28 dB original and 73.21 dB padded; STOI differs from noisy by +0.0000065 on each set. This confirms the fixed preprocessing/de-emphasis/PCM path preserves identity to the expected tolerance. The all-off metric matches noisy without needing a level adjustment; STOI is level-insensitive.','', '## 2. Oracle noise PSD (original Classical, n=14)','', '| Arm | STOI | ΔSTOI vs noisy | ESTOI | ΔESTOI vs noisy |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for arm in ('wiener_on','both_on','oracle_wiener_on','oracle_both_on'):
 x=next(x for x in rd('v11b_factorial_summary.csv') if x['dataset']=='original' and x['arm']==arm)
 lines.append(f"| {arm} | {f(float(x['mean_stoi']))} | {f(float(x['mean_stoi_delta']))} | {f(float(x['mean_estoi']))} | {f(float(x['mean_estoi_delta']))} |")
ps=rd('v11b_oracle_psd_per_file.csv');ratio=[float(x['mean_bin_est_true_psd_ratio']) for x in ps];cont=[float(x['selected_speech_fraction']) for x in ps]
lines += ['', f"Estimated/oracle noise PSD mean bin ratio: {np.mean(ratio):.2f}× (median {np.median(ratio):.2f}×; range {min(ratio):.2f}–{max(ratio):.2f}×). `NoisePsd` selects frames that VAD labels non-speech; it is an average, not a recursive initializer. The first selected frame was clean-speech by the reference mask in 0/14 files, but subsequent selected frames overlap clean speech: mean {100*np.mean(cont):.1f}% (range {100*min(cont):.1f}–{100*max(cont):.1f}%). This is consistent with VAD false negatives contaminating the estimated PSD. Per-file estimates and contamination counts are in [v11b_oracle_psd_per_file.csv](v11b_oracle_psd_per_file.csv).", '', '## 3. STOI/ESTOI change and modulation by SNR bucket','', 'Each value is mean output minus noisy baseline; modulation is output/noisy using the existing noise-only modulation proxy. “—” means the proxy had no qualifying nonspeech run (at least 0.5 s), not a zero ratio. Original audio had no measurable qualifying runs; padded audio did.','', '| Set | Route | SNR dB | n | ΔSTOI | ΔESTOI | Modulation ratio |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in rd('v11b_snr_summary.csv'):
 lines.append(f"| {x['dataset']} | {x['route']} | {int(float(x['snr_db'])):+d} | {x['n']} | {f(float(x['mean_stoi_delta']))} | {f(float(x['mean_estoi_delta']))} | {f(float(x['mean_modulation_ratio']))} |")
lines += ['', 'Actual-route totals by dataset:']
per=rd('v11b_per_file.csv')
lines+=['','| Set | n | Noisy STOI | Output STOI | ΔSTOI | Noisy ESTOI | Output ESTOI | ΔESTOI |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for ds in ('original','padded'):
 q=[x for x in per if x['dataset']==ds]
 lines.append(f"| {ds} | {len(q)} | {f(avg(q,'noisy_stoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'output_stoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'stoi_delta'))} | {f(avg(q,'noisy_estoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'output_estoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'estoi_delta'))} |")
lines += ['', '### Higher-SNR Light touch counterfactual','', 'For the 16 files per dataset at +10/+15 dB, compare current route output against the test-only Light touch output (strict improvement threshold +0.0001 STOI). The output is a recommendation signal, not a routing change.','', '| Set | Better with Light touch | Mean ΔSTOI across all 16 | Mean gain among improved |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
cf=rd('v11b_light_counterfactual.csv')
for ds in ('original','padded'):
 q=[x for x in cf if x['dataset']==ds];better=[x for x in q if float(x['stoi_gain_light'])>1e-4]
 lines.append(f"| {ds} | {len(better)}/{len(q)} | {f(avg(q,'stoi_gain_light'))} | {f(avg(better,'stoi_gain_light'))} |")
lines += ['', '## 4. Brown-hum files vs other Full-route files','', '“Brown hum” is the dataset label for brown-noise interference; it is not a separate sinusoidal hum component. The paired no-brown rows remove the entire brown-noise component and run the Full path test helper with the route parameters held from the noisy input. This is an optimistic clean-input counterfactual, not a deployable route comparison.','', '| Set | Full-route subset | n | STOI | ESTOI | Speech-band SI-SDR vs clean (dB) |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for ds in ('original','padded'):
 for subset in ('brown_hum','other'):
  q=[x for x in per if x['dataset']==ds and x['route']=='Full adaptive' and ((x['noise_type']=='brown_hum')==(subset=='brown_hum'))]
  lines.append(f"| {ds} | {subset} | {len(q)} | {f(avg(q,'output_stoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'output_estoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'speechband_sisdr_db'))} |")
lines += ['', 'Paired brown-noise removal counterfactual:','', '| Set | n | Brown actual STOI | No-brown STOI | Brown actual ESTOI | No-brown ESTOI | Speech-band SI-SDR actual / no-brown (dB) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
h=rd('v11b_brown_hum_per_file.csv')
for ds in ('original','padded'):
 q=[x for x in h if x['dataset']==ds]
 lines.append(f"| {ds} | {len(q)} | {f(avg(q,'brown_actual_stoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'no_brown_stoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'brown_actual_estoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'no_brown_estoi'))} | {f(avg(q,'brown_speechband_sisdr'))} / {f(avg(q,'no_brown_speechband_sisdr'))} |")
lines += ['', '## 5. Ranked candidate fixes (proposals only)','', '1. **Prevent speech leakage into the Classical noise PSD.** Observed estimate/oracle ratio is 12.33× on average; oracle both-stage STOI is +0.045 vs current both-stage output on original Classical (0.9331 vs 0.8883). Risk: conservative masking may leave more residual noise; the oracle is unattainable in production. Confirm with per-file speech-overlap traces and a held-out set, comparing STOI/ESTOI and residual noise.', '2. **Retune the Classical spectral stack, especially the adaptive Wiener component.** Removing the Wiener gain while keeping subtraction and downstream processing raises original Classical STOI by about +0.026 (0.9143 vs 0.8883) and padded by +0.0005 (0.9481 vs 0.9476); Wiener-only is +0.0272 original and +0.0037 padded. Risk: more residual noise, and behavior must remain consistent with the intended Classical spec. Confirm with the same factorial plus listening/residual-noise checks.', '3. **Consider Light touch routing for a subset of +10/+15 dB cases.** Counterfactual Light touch scored higher on 9/16 original and 8/16 padded files; average gain across all 16 was +0.0236 and +0.0054 STOI. Risk: increased residual noise and route changes; confirm on unseen speakers/noise seeds with paired ESTOI and listening.', '4. **Inspect downstream EQ/dynamics on the Classical route.** With spectral stages bypassed, downstream-on drops STOI by 0.0135 original and 0.0164 padded versus all-off. This combined ablation cannot attribute the loss to EQ, compressor, normalization, or pre/de-emphasis individually. Risk: loudness or timbre changes. Confirm by separately toggling each fixed stage, level-matching, and checking clipping and speech-band SI-SDR.', '', '## 6. Artifacts and test evidence','', '- [Per-file actual-route STOI/ESTOI and speech-band SI-SDR](v11b_per_file.csv)', '- [Per-file spectral factorial and oracle results](v11b_factorial_per_file.csv)', '- [Factorial means](v11b_factorial_summary.csv)', '- [Per-file oracle PSD ratio and VAD overlap](v11b_oracle_psd_per_file.csv)', '- [Per-file SNR/modulation metrics](v11b_modulation_per_file.csv)', '- [SNR-bucket means](v11b_snr_summary.csv)', '- [High-SNR Light touch counterfactual](v11b_light_counterfactual.csv)', '- [Brown-hum files and paired no-brown counterfactual](v11b_brown_hum_per_file.csv)', '- Reproducers: `scripts/v11b_metrics.py`, `scripts/v11b_oracle_psd.py`, and Kotlin evaluation-only tests `V11BFactorialTest` / `V11BCounterfactualTest`.', '- Targeted JVM tests: 2 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped after setting `SIGNALCHAIN_ROOT` to the repository root. No production test or source files changed.', '- DNSMOS was not scored: temporary package dependencies installed, but the model download was reset by upstream; PESQ build failed because MSVC is unavailable. ESTOI is included in each metric table as the additional intelligibility metric.', '- Original-set modulation values are N/A because the noise-only proxy requires a contiguous nonspeech span of at least 0.5 s; padded set provides that span. Do not interpret N/A as a favorable or unfavorable change.', '']
(O/'V11B_FOLLOWUP.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
print(O/'V11B_FOLLOWUP.md')
